return {
["10:00"]={"It is one of those cinemas that stay open twenty-four hours a day: it was \003ten in the morning\004 and I went in to forget the cold for a while.","Artificial respiration","Ricardo Piglia"},
["10:01"]={"At \003about ten o’clock\004 in the morning the sun threw a bright dust-laden bar through one of the side windows, and in and out of the beam flies shot like rushing stars.","Of Mice And Men","John Steinbeck"},
["10:02"]={"\00310:02\004, her eyes rested for a split second on every person who came in.","The Sins of the Father","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:03"]={"She passes the FBI Building at \003three minutes past [ten]\004, she passes the Peace Monument at the northwest corner of the Capitol grounds at five minutes past.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:04"]={"On Saturday. November 12. 1955, the Hill Valley Courthouses clock tower was struck by lightning, which poured 1.21 gigawatts of energy into the structure. Time stood still at \00310:04\004 on the clock’s face from that day on.","Back to the Future: Race Through Time","Marc Sumerak"},
["10:05"]={"She passes the FBI Building at three minutes past [ten], she passes the Peace Monument at the northwest corner of the Capitol grounds at \003five minutes past\004.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:06"]={"“All right, Matt, let’s assume that the point of maximum risk is the Capitol itself, at \00310:06\004, right on the steps—what then?”","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:07"]={"\00310:07 a.m.\004 Access letter only, about nonpayment of minimum payment. Try to remember what was looking for. Restart quest for handbag.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["10:08"]={"My watch is always a little fast, I said. “What time do you make it now?”\n“\003Ten eight\004.”\n“Ten eighteen by mine. You see.”","The Quiet American","Graham Greene"},
["10:09"]={"He followed the squeals down a hallway. A wall clock read 8:09-\00310:09\004 Dallas time.","American Tabloid","James Ellroy"},
["10:10"]={"At about ten o’clock the first tiny snowflakes came loitering down and settled on Jill’s arm. \003Ten minutes later\004 they were falling quite thickly. In twenty minutes the ground was noticeably white.","The Silver Chair","C.S. Lewis"},
["10:11"]={"“Fine,” said Florentyna Kane and looked at her watch. It was \00310:11\004. The digits changed—and were replaced by the rate of her heartbeat—72; normal, she thought.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:12"]={"“I’ll take the coffee tray out,” I suggest humbly. As I pick it up I glance again at my watch. \003Ten twelve\004. I wonder if they’ve started the meeting.","The Undomestic Goddess","Sophie Kinsella"},
["10:13"]={"It’s \003ten-thirteen\004, announced Clancy. “In two more minutes—”\n“Post time,” I said.","The Anthem Sprinters","Ray Bradbury"},
["10:14"]={"\00310:14\004, would her next appointment have to be with Mr. Brett Elders?","The Sins of the Father","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:16"]={"\00310:16\004 At last. Forty minutes of hard work and I have made precisely one bed. I’m way behind. But never mind. Just keep moving. Laundry next.","The Undomestic Goddess","Sophie Kinsella"},
["10:17"]={"Pacey hummed to himself as he walked slowly toward Abel’s office for their daily ten o’clock meeting. It was \003seventeen minutes past ten\004.","Kane & Abel","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:18"]={"I know that it was \00310:18\004 when I got home because I look at my watch a lot.","Extremely Loud and Incredibly Close","Jonathan Safran Foer"},
["10:20"]={"One Monday, at \003twenty past ten in the morning\004, Amaranta was dressing Aureliano José when she heard the distant sound of a crowd and a bugle call","100 years of loneliness","Gabriel García Márquez"},
["10:21"]={"Liz Headleand stares into the mirror, as though entranced. She does not see herself or the objects on her dressing-table. The clock abruptly jerks to \00310:21\004.","The Radiant Way","Margaret Drabble"},
["10:22"]={"Seb looked up at the vast black minute hand on the clock that bounced forward every sixty seconds: \00310:22\004. Was all the work Cedric had put in going to be for nothing?","Be Careful What You Wish For","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:23"]={"The date was the 14th of May and the clock on his desk said the time was \003twenty three minutes past ten\004, so he tapped in the numbers 10:23. At least, that’s what he meant to do. In fact he typed in the numbers 10:03","Ctrl-Z","Andrew Norriss"},
["10:24"]={"Arnet entered the Peabody Wildlife Management Area at \00310:24 A.M.\004, crested a ridge, and noticed fresh skid marks leading to dark, pool-like stains near the side of the road.","Labyrinth","Mark T. Sullivan"},
["10:25"]={"\00310:25\004: Phone call from Lüding, very worked up, urging me to return at once and get in touch with Alois, who was equally worked up.","The Lost Honour of Katharina Blum","Heinrich Böll"},
["10:26"]={"In the exact centre of my visual field was the alarm clock, hands pointing to \003ten-twenty-six\004. An alarm clock I received as a memento of somebody’s wedding.","Hard-Boiled Wonderland and the End of the World","Haruki Murakami"},
["10:27"]={"Mr. Harcourt woke up with mysterious suddenness at \003twenty-seven minutes past 10\004, and, by a curious coincidence, it was at that very instant that the butler came in with two footmen laden with trays of whisky, brandy, syphons, glasses, and biscuits.","England, Their England","A.G. Macdonell"},
["10:30"]={"He checked on Anderson and saw she was still sleeping like a stone. Gardener had decided to wake Bobbi up by \003ten-thirty\004 if she hadn’t awakened on her own.","The Tommyknockers","Stephen King"},
["10:31"]={"Inspector Sanderson has told us that he examined the safe at \00310:31 a.m.\004 and found two good-sized drops of blood on the bottom.","The Red Thumb Mark","R. Austin Freeman"},
["10:32"]={"It was \003ten thirty-two\004 when the bus finally rolled into view.\nThe bus that came was a new type, not like the one I used to take to high school.","Blind Willow, Sleeping Woman","Haruki Murakami"},
["10:33"]={"The time checks out. December 12, \00310:33 A.M.\004 James says the caller disguised their voice. We found a commercial voice changer at the house, in her bedroom.","The Big Law","Chuck Logan"},
["10:34"]={"\00310:34 a.m.\004 on 198.088, the lights went out in Labrador, and the backup generators came on, but Labrador’s sunline stayed off.","Aurora","Kim Stanley Robinson"},
["10:35"]={"It was \00310:35\004 and Brenda Pridmore, at the reception desk at the rear of the main hall of Hoggart’s Laboratory, watched wide-eyed while Inspector Blakelock drew toward him the first labeled bag of exhibits from the clunch pit murder.","Death of an Expert Witness","P.D. James"},
["10:36"]={"Strand post mark and dispatched \003ten thirty-six\004, said Holmes reading it over and over. “Mr. Overton was evidently considerably excited when he sent it over and somewhat incoherent in consequence.”","The Adventure of the Missing Three-Quarter","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle"},
["10:37"]={"I quite agree with you, said Mr. Murbles. “It is a most awkward situation. Lady Dormer died at precisely \00310:37 a.m.\004 on November 11th.”","The Unpleasantness at the Bellona Club","Dorothy L. Sayers"},
["10:38"]={"\00310:38 A.M.\004\nWinston Bartlett was not finding himself entirely satisfied with the way things were going. As he looked her over, he had a lot on his mind. This was the woman who shared his rare blood type and could represent his last hope.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover"},
["10:39"]={"However, I can’t allow you to pay for my travel expenses, as we are strangers and nothing may come of our meeting. My flight arrives at \00310:39 a.m.\004","Duncan’s Bride","Linda Howard"},
["10:40"]={"\003Ten-forty in the morning\004 is hardly an appropriate time to begin imbibing, so I suggest you take it with you. I don’t suppose you’ll be staying long.","The Private Patient","P.D. James"},
["10:41"]={"An old man in a condominium apartment facing the sea was looking out his sixth-floor window at the time of the explosion and was able to fix the time of it at precisely \00310:41\004 Eastern Daylight Time.","Cinnamon Skin","John D. MacDonald"},
["10:42"]={"Ellis scanned the wall-mounted clocks spanning four time zones. The local time read \00310:42\004. Had word of his gaffe already gone all the way to Trimble?","Sold on a Monday","Kristina McMorris"},
["10:43"]={"24 January, \00310:43 a.m\004: one month and two days later I wonder if I should worry about the fact that my darling boyfriend bought me a birthday present that has the potential to cause instant death…","The Wish List","Jane Costello"},
["10:44"]={"At the words, “One thousand pounds to the person who unmasks Lady Whistledown,” the clock read \003forty-four minutes past ten\004.","Romancing Mr. Bridgerton","Julia Quinn"},
["10:45"]={"They reached King’s Cross at a \003quarter to eleven\004. Mr. Weasley dashed across the road to get trolleys for their trunks and they all hurried into the station.","Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets","J.K. Rowling"},
["10:46"]={"OLIVE: [At KATHERINE’S elbow—examining her watch on its stand] It’s \003fourteen minutes to eleven\004.\nKATHERINE: Olive, Olive!\nOLIVE: I just wanted to see the time.","The Mob","John Galsworthy"},
["10:47"]={"\00310:47 a.m.\004 I’ll just send him a tiny friendly message, nothing flirtatious, just to restore good relations.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["10:48"]={"At \00310:48 am\004, I closed my folder but didn’t bother putting it back in my bag, so you knew I was on my way to a committee or meeting room nearby. Before I stood up, I folded my paper napkin and put it and the spoon into my coffee cup, a neat sort of person, you thought.","Apple Tree Yard","Louise Doughty"},
["10:49"]={"\00310:49 A.M.\004\nAs Ally watched Winston Bartlett sweep from the room, she was still trying to take measure of the man. What troubled her was why Grant and Bartlett were both so anxious to get her and her mother out to the clinic.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover"},
["10:50"]={"The Rt. Hon. the Lord Barrington of Bristol Docklands was to arrive at St. Paul’s Cathedral at \00310:50\004 on the morning of April 10th, 1992.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:51"]={"... but he still remained confident that they could make it to the top when they reached 27,550 feet at \00310:51\004. That was when he heard a cry that sounded like a wounded animal. He knew it wasn’t Finch.","Paths of Glory","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:52"]={"It was now \003eight minutes to eleven\004, and he began to feel rather cross and impatient. There was nothing to do in the big, ugly, stately room into which he had been shown.","From Out of the Vasty Deep","Marie Belloc Lowndes"},
["10:53"]={"He begins to make a record of our observations. “\00310:53 hrs\004,” he writes, as we crouch at the top of the stairs, listening to his mother in the hall below.","Spies","Michael Frayn"},
["10:54"]={"I’m telling you that you paid 6,495 into Bennington’s Bank in the High Street at \00310:54 a.m.\004 today, insisted Frost.\n“And I’m telling you I did not” spat the man.","Hard Frost","R.D. Wingfield"},
["10:55"]={"At \00310:55\004 they would enter the Farholme Gate, emerging a mere ten and a half minutes later at Bannermere Gate. Forty light-years away.","The Shadow and Night","Chris Walley"},
["10:56"]={"BOOTH WATSON KNEW IT WOULD be a question of careful timing if he hoped to pull it off. He’d have to keep one eye on the clock to make sure it was \00310:56\004 before he made his move.","Next in Line","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:57"]={"At 10:55, the canon would accompany the Lord Chancellor into the cathedral, and then they would proceed to the front of the nave where he should land— the canon’s word— at \00310:57\004.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["10:58"]={"One day Joe was sitting in the office waiting for his 11 o’clock appointment, and at \00310:58\004 this black gal came in.","Lightning Rods","Helen DeWitt"},
["10:59"]={"She had just returned from the only shopping she needed to do that day, and it was still \003a minute before eleven\004.","That Hideous Strength","C.S. Lewis"},
